  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Men and women, especially the youth and other groups at  risk of vulnerability or marginalization, acquire appropriate competencies and have access to and engage in remunerative and productive work.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PHL 101 supports the Philippine Labor and Employment Plan (LEP) 2023 to 2028, contributing to Priority 1 on maximizing productive, remunerative, freely chosen, and sustainable work. It aims to increase employability, expand access to employment, and promote shared labour market governance. The strategy strengthens active labour market programs (ALMPs), skills development, and labour market information systems (LMIS), targeting youth, women, and vulnerable groups. It also aligns with the National Technical Education and Skills Development Plan (NTESDP) 2023 to 2028, advancing modern, inclusive, and high-quality technical and vocational education and training (TVET). Key interventions include promoting women in STEM, enhancing equity and quality in TVET, and improving public-private collaboration in skills financing and delivery. The CPO also supports digitalization of public employment services and LMIS, assessment of youth employability programs, and emergency employment for coconut sector rehabilitation. It contributes to labour statistics development, including pilots on the new work concept, informal economy, green jobs supporting the Philippine Statistical Development Program (PSDP) 2023 to 2029 and the UN Sustainable Development Cooperation Framework (UNSDCF) 2024 to 2028, particularly Output 1 on inclusive, resilient, and quality learning environment and Outcome 2 on decent work. Implementation involves collaboration with national government agencies, employers and workers organizations, and development partners.</narrative>
  </description>
